{"result": {"response": {"id": "chatcmpl-78d5a47e-2072-9c5e-ae8e-f6f1f7976099", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "logprobs": null, "message": {"content": "{\n    \"title\": \"吸入性与鼻内糖皮质激素药物相互作用及不良反应社区\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on inhaled and intranasal corticosteroids—including 氟替卡松, 倍氯米松, 莫米松, 环索奈德, and 丙酸氟替卡松—and their associations with systemic adverse reactions, particularly when co-administered with CYP3A4 strong inhibitors such as protease inhibitors (e.g., 达芦那韦/利托那韦). These drugs are indicated for conditions like seasonal allergies and are grouped under the drug classes 吸入性糖皮质激素 and 鼻内糖皮质激素. Key adverse effects include 医源性库欣综合征, HPA轴抑制, 肾上腺功能异常, 口咽部假丝酵母菌病, 发音障碍, and 接触性超敏反应. The data highlight significant pharmacokinetic interactions that elevate systemic exposure and adverse event risk.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氟替卡松 is strongly linked to multiple systemic adverse reactions\",\n            \"explanation\": \"氟替卡松 demonstrates documented associations with several serious systemic adverse effects, including 肾上腺功能异常, 全身不良反应, and abnormal results on 皮质醇刺激试验. A meta-analysis of five randomized trials involving 732 adult patients showed that daily doses of 500–2000 μg of 氟替卡松 were associated with adrenal dysfunction rates ranging from 6% to 13% [Data: Relationships (12743)]. Additionally, evidence indicates that co-administration with CYP3A4 inhibitors can significantly increase systemic exposure, thereby elevating the risk of adverse drug reactions [Data: Relationships (12740, 2519)]. These findings underscore the importance of dose monitoring and potential drug interaction screening when prescribing 氟替卡松.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Multiple corticosteroids interact with CYP3A4 strong inhibitors, increasing systemic toxicity risk\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Several corticosteroids in this community—包括 倍氯米松, 莫米松, 环索奈德, and 氟替卡松—are metabolized via CYP3A4 and exhibit clinically significant interactions with CYP3A4 strong inhibitors such as protease inhibitors (e.g., 达芦那韦/利托那韦). These interactions can lead to markedly increased systemic exposure and a heightened risk of iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome and other systemic adverse effects [Data: Relationships (29432, 50064, 44171)]. Literature reviews confirm that these drug combinations have been increasingly reported to cause drug interaction–related iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome, especially in patients with HIV receiving protease inhibitor–based antiretroviral therapy [Data: Relationships (29432, +more)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"医源性库欣综合征 is a critical systemic adverse effect tied to corticosteroid–CYP3A4 inhibitor co-administration\",\n            \"explanation\": \"医源性库欣综合征 emerges as a severe systemic adverse reaction primarily when inhaled or intranasal corticosteroids are used concomitantly with CYP3A4 inhibitors. While standalone use of these corticosteroids rarely causes this condition, combination therapy—especially with ritonavir-boosted protease inhibitors—has led to numerous case reports. A 2013 review identified 51 cases of iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome in HIV-positive patients using ICS/INCS with protease inhibitors, with 94% involving ritonavir-containing regimens [Data: Relationships (1055, 17505)]. This highlights a high-risk drug interaction scenario requiring clinical vigilance and potential regimen adjustments.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"吸入性糖皮质激素 class is associated with both local and systemic adverse effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The drug class 吸入性糖皮质激素 is linked to a spectrum of adverse reactions, ranging from local effects like 口咽部假丝酵母菌病 and 发音障碍 to systemic issues such as HPA轴抑制 and 医源性库欣综合征. These associations are particularly pronounced when these agents are combined with CYP3A4 inhibitors [Data: Relationships (10116, 10114, 10118, 10110)]. Although generally considered safe at recommended doses, recent evidence shows that metabolic interactions can shift the risk-benefit profile, necessitating alternative therapies (e.g., leukotriene receptor antagonists or antihistamines) in high-risk patients [Data: Relationships (10110)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"达芦那韦/利托那韦 acts as a CYP3A4 strong inhibitor affecting corticosteroid metabolism\",\n            \"explanation\": \"达芦那韦/利托那韦, classified as a protease inhibitor, functions as a potent CYP3A4 inhibitor and is implicated in increasing systemic exposure to corticosteroids metabolized by this enzyme pathway. Evidence notes that ritonavir-boosted regimens (like LPV/r) are frequently involved in drug interaction–induced iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome when co-administered with inhaled or intranasal corticosteroids [Data: Relationships (59169)]. In a case series, 48 out of 51 patients with iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome were on ritonavir-containing therapy, underscoring its central role in this interaction network [Data: Relationships (1055)]. This positions 达芦那韦/利托那韦 as a key modulator of risk within this pharmacological community.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"丙酸氟替卡松 is a specific agent within the 吸入性糖皮质激素 class with documented interaction risks\",\n            \"explanation\": \"丙酸氟替卡松 is explicitly categorized under the 吸入性糖皮质激素 drug class and has been studied in the context of drug interactions leading to iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome. In pediatric and adult HIV patients, average daily doses of inhaled fluticasone propionate often exceeded recommended limits when used with ritonavir-based regimens, contributing to adverse outcomes [Data: Relationships (55313)]. The data indicate that even standard doses of nasal fluticasone propionate may pose risks when combined with strong CYP3A4 inhibitors, reinforcing the need for dose adjustment or therapeutic substitution in vulnerable populations [Data: Relationships (55313)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Local adverse effects are common across corticosteroid formulations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Local adverse reactions—including 口咽部假丝酵母菌病 (oral candidiasis), 发音障碍 (dysphonia), and 接触性超敏反应 (contact hypersensitivity)—are consistently reported with 吸入性糖皮质激素 use. These effects occur even in the absence of systemic interactions and represent well-documented limitations of topical corticosteroid delivery [Data: Relationships (10116, 10114, 10118)]. While generally less severe than systemic reactions, they impact patient adherence and quality of life, warranting preventive measures such as mouth rinsing post-inhalation.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a high clinical impact due to the potential for severe systemic adverse reactions—particularly iatrogenic Cushing’s syndrome and adrenal dysfunction—when commonly prescribed corticosteroids are co-administered with CYP3A4 inhibitors like ritonavir-boosted antiretrovirals.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782127004, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1706, "prompt_tokens": 7418, "total_tokens": 9124, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"吸入性与鼻内糖皮质激素药物相互作用及不良反应社区\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on inhaled and intranasal corticosteroids—including 氟替卡松, 倍氯米松, 莫米松, 环索奈德, and 丙酸氟替卡松—and their associations with systemic adverse reactions, particularly when co-administered with CYP3A4 strong inhibitors such as protease inhibitors (e.g., 达芦那韦/利托那韦). These drugs are indicated for conditions like seasonal allergi